1
00:00:00,470 --> 00:00:01,810
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,810 --> 00:00:03,270
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:09,450 --> 00:00:11,320
(Kang Da Mi, My Youngest)

4
00:00:26,870 --> 00:00:27,870
Ms. Jo.

5
00:00:29,270 --> 00:00:30,900
Please call Professor Yoo. Quickly.

6
00:00:30,970 --> 00:00:32,270
Yes, Dr. Ju. Just a moment.

7
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:38,980
It hurts so, so much.

8
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:40,750
It hurts.

9
00:00:42,150 --> 00:00:43,450
If I'd known it would be like this,

10
00:00:44,650 --> 00:00:45,980
I would've brought...

11
00:00:47,120 --> 00:00:48,790
someone from my family.

12
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:51,120
I'm scared.

13
00:00:51,190 --> 00:00:54,030
Ms. Jo, straighten your body
and lie down for a moment.

14
00:00:55,130 --> 00:00:56,130
Slowly.

15
00:00:57,860 --> 00:01:00,430
I am going to examine your abdomen.

16
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:03,030
Tell me if it hurts too much. Okay.

17
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:07,070
(Episode 42)

18
00:01:08,440 --> 00:01:12,510
Aunt Da Mi.
Until I fall asleep again,

19
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:13,910
you have to keep carrying me
on your back.

20
00:01:14,710 --> 00:01:16,410
You cannot leave Su Ah behind.

21
00:01:17,250 --> 00:01:20,220
Okay. I'm right here with you,

22
00:01:20,350 --> 00:01:22,090
so do not cry
and go to sleep now, Su Ah.

23
00:01:23,990 --> 00:01:25,760
- Aunt Da Mi.
- Yes?

24
00:01:26,790 --> 00:01:28,030
I miss Mom.

25
00:01:30,960 --> 00:01:34,470
You must really miss
your mom, Su Ah.

26
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:38,940
I came because I missed Mom, too.

27
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:41,170
I understand how you feel.

28
00:01:50,580 --> 00:01:53,950
- You're here?
- Yes, Aunt Ri Ja.

29
00:01:56,150 --> 00:01:57,820
Where did Gang Nam go?

30
00:01:59,220 --> 00:02:01,660
He barely pretended to help out...

31
00:02:02,190 --> 00:02:03,760
before running off,
saying he had an errand.

32
00:02:04,630 --> 00:02:05,660
What about Dae Chi?

33
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:08,570
He also left earlier,
saying he had urgent business.

34
00:02:08,930 --> 00:02:11,170
Did you call your mom?

35
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:14,370
Yes, I kept calling,
but she didn't answer,

36
00:02:14,570 --> 00:02:15,640
so I stopped by out of concern.

37
00:02:16,510 --> 00:02:19,340
Did she really go dancing
somewhere or what?

38
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:22,750
Ever since she bought
that yellow dress,

39
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:24,250
she has been acting really strange.

40
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:29,450
Hey, your mom's really fallen
for someone.

41
00:02:31,220 --> 00:02:34,930
Why would Mom fall for someone?
What's this about dancing?

42
00:02:35,190 --> 00:02:37,100
Ask your mom yourself.

43
00:02:37,430 --> 00:02:38,860
It came straight out
of her own mouth.

44
00:02:40,870 --> 00:02:42,770
Hey, Su Ah is asleep.

45
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:45,270
Go lay her down in that room...

46
00:02:45,670 --> 00:02:47,440
and do the dishes while you're here
before you leave.

47
00:02:49,310 --> 00:02:51,640
I was running around the restaurant
all day by myself,

48
00:02:52,210 --> 00:02:54,310
and I don't even have the energy
to lift a finger.

49
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:03,560
Fallen for someone?

50
00:03:04,490 --> 00:03:05,920
No way.

51
00:03:08,060 --> 00:03:10,530
Did she get another thing
to worry about?

52
00:03:14,100 --> 00:03:17,840
- I'm going home.
- I told you to stay...

53
00:03:17,970 --> 00:03:19,800
the night at our place, Mom.

54
00:03:21,140 --> 00:03:22,670
I don't really want
to go back either...

55
00:03:22,810 --> 00:03:24,610
because I feel guilty toward Ms. Jo.

56
00:03:25,180 --> 00:03:27,450
Even so, how could I sleep here?

57
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:29,410
Who is Ms. Jo, Dad?

58
00:03:31,050 --> 00:03:34,890
If you feel really uncomfortable,
you should go, Mother.

59
00:03:35,450 --> 00:03:38,020
Please come see Ye Ri again,
anytime you feel like it.

60
00:03:39,090 --> 00:03:40,590
Honey, take her home.

61
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:42,160
Okay.

62
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:44,800
Then before you go, Mom,

63
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:47,330
let's take at least one picture
together, all right?

64
00:03:48,300 --> 00:03:49,470
What picture?

65
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:53,140
Honestly, today feels like
a dream to me.

66
00:03:53,370 --> 00:03:55,810
Ye Ri got to greet you properly
for the first time, too.

67
00:03:56,170 --> 00:03:57,710
Let us take one together, okay?

68
00:03:57,840 --> 00:04:00,810
Looking back on life,
photos are all that remain, right?

69
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:04,920
Yes. Ye Ri, take a picture
with Grandma. Go sit down.

70
00:04:04,980 --> 00:04:06,420
- Come here.
- Okay.

71
00:04:07,350 --> 00:04:08,350
What about you, Mom?

72
00:04:08,850 --> 00:04:10,120
Me too?

73
00:04:13,390 --> 00:04:15,490
Honey, you are good
at taking photos.

74
00:04:15,830 --> 00:04:18,600
To get our whole family in the shot,

75
00:04:18,660 --> 00:04:20,770
stretch your arm out
and take it, okay?

76
00:04:20,830 --> 00:04:22,300
Come on, come here.

77
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,100
- Sit down.
- Here we go.

78
00:04:25,370 --> 00:04:27,940
What on earth is this...

79
00:04:28,370 --> 00:04:33,040
Okay, smile everyone.
One, two, three. Smile.

80
00:04:48,330 --> 00:04:51,500
How dare you try to cross this gate?

81
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:54,430
On the way, I heard you talking
to my sister-in-law on the phone.

82
00:04:55,130 --> 00:04:56,130
She said Mi Mi went somewhere,

83
00:04:56,270 --> 00:04:58,340
has not come home,
and is out of reach.

84
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:01,070
Let me just walk you
to the courtyard.

85
00:05:01,570 --> 00:05:02,940
Not a chance.

86
00:05:03,310 --> 00:05:05,810
I held back in your house
because Ye Ri was watching.

87
00:05:06,110 --> 00:05:07,280
But do not even dream of it.

88
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:14,450
If she runs into you this time,
she might just knock your teeth out.

89
00:05:15,590 --> 00:05:16,850
Knock my teeth out?

90
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:23,090
Okay. Then your useless son
will take his leave...

91
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:24,930
as soon as I see you go inside.

92
00:05:28,630 --> 00:05:31,100
If you ever feel sick again,
call me right away, Mom.

93
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:32,300
All right?

94
00:05:39,980 --> 00:05:40,980
Hey, little sister.

95
00:05:42,380 --> 00:05:44,020
You do not think Mom...

96
00:05:45,080 --> 00:05:46,680
ran away from home, do you?

97
00:05:47,820 --> 00:05:50,660
It would not be surprising
if she did.

98
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:53,260
Just think of all the grief
we put her through.

99
00:05:54,860 --> 00:05:56,030
Ran away?

100
00:05:56,690 --> 00:06:01,430
- Wait, did she run away from home?
- Grandma, you are back?

101
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,300
Mrs. Choi.

102
00:06:03,970 --> 00:06:07,270
Where on earth have you been,
only coming back just now?

103
00:06:07,540 --> 00:06:08,870
Running the place alone,

104
00:06:08,940 --> 00:06:11,440
I almost died
before even getting married.

105
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:13,240
Where is Su Ah?

106
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:15,080
She fell asleep,
so I put her down in your room.

107
00:06:17,080 --> 00:06:21,090
By the way, Grandma,
do you think Mom really found a man?

108
00:06:22,020 --> 00:06:23,450
I swear, I definitely saw him.

109
00:06:23,550 --> 00:06:25,590
Did you just see the guys
from the business association?

110
00:06:25,890 --> 00:06:27,590
Mom attends
those meetings sometimes.

111
00:06:27,760 --> 00:06:31,600
He was tall and good-looking.

112
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:32,660
On top of that,

113
00:06:34,200 --> 00:06:35,200
he was even young.

114
00:06:36,130 --> 00:06:37,740
There is no way
he is from that group.

115
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:40,070
A gigolo.

116
00:06:40,740 --> 00:06:43,070
My sister got tangled up
with a gigolo.

117
00:06:43,170 --> 00:06:45,840
The one who gets seduced
by gigolos every time...

118
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:49,450
and loses all her money
is you, Mona Ri Ja.

119
00:06:50,080 --> 00:06:52,280
Mi Mi would never in a million years
fall for that.

120
00:06:52,350 --> 00:06:53,680
Watch your mouth.

121
00:06:54,020 --> 00:06:58,190
We came from the same womb,
so I was just wondering.

122
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:04,230
Da Mi, what is it?

123
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:14,440
Right, if she had actually
run away from home,

124
00:07:14,870 --> 00:07:16,540
she would have packed a bag first.

125
00:07:16,740 --> 00:07:18,580
Mom did not run away
from home, Auntie.

126
00:07:18,640 --> 00:07:20,080
Everything is still here.

127
00:07:21,110 --> 00:07:22,910
Did Mom really say
she was staying out all night?

128
00:07:23,350 --> 00:07:28,990
- Would I make that up?
- Not that you made it up,

129
00:07:29,150 --> 00:07:31,460
but you tend to exaggerate.

130
00:07:36,530 --> 00:07:39,560
I knew there was a good reason
I found her so irritating.

131
00:07:43,230 --> 00:07:44,600
Did she pack her bags?

132
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:49,210
No, Grandma.
She must have had an errand to run.

133
00:07:49,970 --> 00:07:53,040
Or maybe she was upset
and went out to get some fresh air.

134
00:07:54,450 --> 00:07:55,980
It is all my fault.

135
00:07:58,120 --> 00:07:59,250
Why would you say that, Grandma?

136
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:03,920
Oh, right, you do not know.

137
00:08:04,820 --> 00:08:06,190
You see, the truth is...

138
00:08:06,420 --> 00:08:07,890
Do you know who showed up...

139
00:08:07,960 --> 00:08:11,300
- in front of your mom?
- Ri Ja.

140
00:08:14,170 --> 00:08:15,930
Yes, Mrs. Choi.

141
00:08:17,740 --> 00:08:19,540
Who showed up?

142
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:22,370
Hey, Kkangda. It is getting late.

143
00:08:22,870 --> 00:08:23,940
Do you want me
to give you a ride home?

144
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:25,810
No, I am staying over tonight.

145
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:27,580
I will wait until Mom gets home
before I leave.

146
00:08:27,750 --> 00:08:30,150
Yes, that is a good idea.

147
00:08:30,950 --> 00:08:35,090
Seeing you here
will cheer your mom up.

148
00:08:49,630 --> 00:08:52,000
Mom must have cleaned
this room every day.

149
00:08:52,670 --> 00:08:54,110
There is not a speck of dust.

150
00:09:02,380 --> 00:09:03,380
Oh, right.

151
00:09:04,050 --> 00:09:06,180
I completely forgot
I left this behind.

152
00:09:16,290 --> 00:09:19,630
Mom, I missed you, so I came home.

153
00:09:19,830 --> 00:09:20,830
Where are you?

154
00:09:21,530 --> 00:09:22,600
Did you have dinner?

155
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:25,240
Come home soon. I will be waiting.

156
00:09:28,810 --> 00:09:30,270
(Mom, I missed you, so I came home.
Where are you?)

157
00:09:30,340 --> 00:09:31,880
(Did you eat dinner?
Come home soon. I will be waiting.)

158
00:09:40,820 --> 00:09:42,850
This is really strange.

159
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:45,020
Why hasn't she
even read my text yet?

160
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:47,730
Shoot, I am going to be late.

161
00:09:49,030 --> 00:09:51,030
Hey, Kkangda. Hold on.

162
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:55,900
- What is it? I am late right now.
- Look, about Mom.

163
00:09:56,630 --> 00:09:58,970
Seeing those people
back in the neighborhood...

164
00:09:59,100 --> 00:10:02,710
must have been such a shock
that it drove her a little crazy,

165
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:04,440
and I think she might really
have fallen for someone.

166
00:10:05,740 --> 00:10:07,850
Those people? Who?

167
00:10:10,550 --> 00:10:13,580
- Kang Hak Sung.
- Dad's back?

168
00:10:14,120 --> 00:10:15,850
Who is Dad, you idiot?

169
00:10:17,890 --> 00:10:19,260
Well, with that woman...

170
00:10:19,620 --> 00:10:20,660
They went completely
broke together...

171
00:10:20,730 --> 00:10:22,530
and apparently moved back
to our neighborhood.

172
00:10:24,130 --> 00:10:25,430
That woman had the nerve to work...

173
00:10:25,500 --> 00:10:27,830
at the hospital
across from our restaurant,

174
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:31,800
and Auntie ran right into her.
She nearly tore her hair out.

175
00:10:32,940 --> 00:10:34,840
When did this happen?

176
00:10:36,010 --> 00:10:38,440
A few days ago. But...

177
00:10:39,040 --> 00:10:42,010
Mom has definitely been acting
weird ever since.

178
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:43,280
How can they be so shameless?

179
00:10:43,350 --> 00:10:44,950
How could they move
into our neighborhood?

180
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:46,220
Tell me about it.

181
00:10:46,620 --> 00:10:48,420
I'm so worried about Mom.

182
00:10:49,290 --> 00:10:50,920
Hey, you are late.

183
00:10:51,620 --> 00:10:54,360
- Worry on your way to work. Run.
- Right, okay.

184
00:10:54,430 --> 00:10:56,190
Call me as soon as Mom gets home.

185
00:11:09,740 --> 00:11:11,640
She used to come in
at the crack of dawn...

186
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:13,580
and clean the whole place,
so where is she?

187
00:11:18,120 --> 00:11:19,120
To be honest...

188
00:11:19,850 --> 00:11:21,220
I like Kang Da Mi, Seung Yun.

189
00:11:25,760 --> 00:11:26,760
Right.

190
00:11:31,230 --> 00:11:34,000
Wait, did she run off
just because I scolded her a bit?

191
00:11:38,300 --> 00:11:41,240
(Kang Da Mi)

192
00:11:48,010 --> 00:11:49,010
Team Leader Cha.

193
00:11:49,110 --> 00:11:51,650
Working out together today
was really great in so many ways.

194
00:11:52,050 --> 00:11:54,150
We even talked business.
Two birds with one stone.

195
00:11:54,250 --> 00:11:56,420
- Really?
- Hello.

196
00:11:56,450 --> 00:11:57,460
Kang Da Mi.

197
00:11:57,990 --> 00:11:58,990
Good timing.

198
00:12:00,830 --> 00:12:02,130
Here, this is for you.

199
00:12:02,490 --> 00:12:06,560
- No, that is okay, Team Leader Cha.
- Take it. I bought it for you.

200
00:12:07,700 --> 00:12:10,770
I know you cannot drink coffee,
so I got you peppermint tea.

201
00:12:11,570 --> 00:12:14,340
Thank you. I missed breakfast today.

202
00:12:14,640 --> 00:12:16,710
Is that so? Then...

203
00:12:19,380 --> 00:12:20,380
Take this, too.

204
00:12:20,780 --> 00:12:23,450
I got it from a hotel bakery,
so it should be good.

205
00:12:23,750 --> 00:12:26,350
Assistant Manager Kang
already tried it and recommended it.

206
00:12:29,650 --> 00:12:32,520
That is right, Da Mi.
It is really expensive. Top quality.

207
00:12:33,460 --> 00:12:35,890
Yes, thank you. I will enjoy it.

208
00:12:36,030 --> 00:12:37,030
Kang Da Mi.

209
00:12:39,500 --> 00:12:40,760
What are you doing
standing around here?

210
00:12:40,830 --> 00:12:42,100
You are late right now. Late.

211
00:12:42,830 --> 00:12:44,000
Good morning, Head Designer Cha.

212
00:12:45,900 --> 00:12:47,370
Actually, there is still
one minute left.

213
00:12:48,540 --> 00:12:49,540
One...

214
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:51,880
One minute left?

215
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:55,850
Wait, how can an assistant
show up right on the dot...

216
00:12:55,910 --> 00:12:58,080
and think that is acceptable?
With that attitude?

217
00:12:58,350 --> 00:12:59,980
Besides, the office is filthy
right now.

218
00:13:00,050 --> 00:13:01,520
Hurry up and go clean it.

219
00:13:02,550 --> 00:13:03,550
Yes, sir.

220
00:13:08,660 --> 00:13:09,930
Why are you glaring at me,
Team Leader Cha?

221
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:13,360
I only have one minute left,
so I have to get going.

222
00:13:14,830 --> 00:13:16,930
Gosh, only buying drinks
for himself?

223
00:13:30,510 --> 00:13:31,520
Team Leader Cha.

224
00:13:33,080 --> 00:13:36,650
Did you not buy that sandwich
for us to share?

225
00:13:37,020 --> 00:13:38,860
Well, yes, but...

226
00:13:39,390 --> 00:13:41,360
Kang Da Mi said
she skipped breakfast.

227
00:13:43,160 --> 00:13:44,160
Why?

228
00:13:45,300 --> 00:13:46,360
Are your feelings hurt?

229
00:13:46,730 --> 00:13:48,370
Of course not.

230
00:13:49,030 --> 00:13:51,240
I was actually about
to give her mine.

231
00:13:51,670 --> 00:13:53,270
You just beat me to it,
Team Leader Cha.

232
00:13:54,170 --> 00:13:55,670
You must be hungry, too.

233
00:13:56,940 --> 00:13:59,080
Yes, working out made me hungry.

234
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:01,750
If you do not mind,

235
00:14:01,910 --> 00:14:03,010
could you share,
Assistant Manager Kang?

236
00:14:03,110 --> 00:14:05,650
Yes, Team Leader Cha.
I would love that.

237
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:07,520
Let us share it together.

238
00:14:08,450 --> 00:14:09,450
Thank you.

239
00:14:10,020 --> 00:14:13,560
Let us see,
something to cut it with...

240
00:14:14,090 --> 00:14:15,460
Oh, there must be something
in the pantry.

241
00:14:15,630 --> 00:14:16,630
I will go get it.

242
00:14:23,330 --> 00:14:25,670
I cannot believe a day would come
that I would thank Manager Kang.

243
00:14:42,420 --> 00:14:45,320
You really take the cake
when it comes to having no manners.

244
00:14:45,860 --> 00:14:47,290
You asked to meet...

245
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:49,660
and then kept your elder waiting
for 30 whole minutes.

246
00:14:50,560 --> 00:14:51,560
You are right.

247
00:14:52,430 --> 00:14:54,770
I have always lacked manners
since I was little.

248
00:14:54,830 --> 00:14:55,900
No respect either.

249
00:14:56,970 --> 00:14:59,500
Probably because
I grew up so sheltered.

250
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:01,010
Thanks to you, Aunt.

251
00:15:03,740 --> 00:15:07,410
You must be scared
now that I said I would find Da Mi.

252
00:15:08,380 --> 00:15:11,620
I was ready to do whatever I wanted
and stir up some real drama.

253
00:15:11,980 --> 00:15:12,980
Why did you call me here?

254
00:15:13,820 --> 00:15:14,820
Aunt.

255
00:15:15,450 --> 00:15:17,420
I really was going to give you
three million dollars...

256
00:15:17,450 --> 00:15:18,990
and cut all ties with you.

257
00:15:20,690 --> 00:15:23,160
But because we're blood relatives...

258
00:15:23,230 --> 00:15:25,660
and lived together all those years,

259
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,130
I just couldn't turn my back
on you completely.

260
00:15:29,830 --> 00:15:31,140
That is why I asked you to come.

261
00:15:33,770 --> 00:15:37,040
I'm sorry I blocked your number.
And...

262
00:15:37,540 --> 00:15:38,840
I will keep giving you money.

263
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:41,810
You know,

264
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:44,380
you are the only real family
I have left.

265
00:15:45,550 --> 00:15:48,320
Getting older must have taught you
something after all.

266
00:15:49,450 --> 00:15:51,090
Fine, how much are you giving me?

267
00:15:51,860 --> 00:15:53,820
I will give you
5,000 dollars each month.

268
00:15:54,490 --> 00:15:55,490
What?

269
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:00,500
Just give me
300,000 dollars at once.

270
00:16:01,130 --> 00:16:02,130
Not three million dollars,

271
00:16:03,930 --> 00:16:06,300
just 300,000 dollars.

272
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:08,840
Then I will never ask you
for a dime again.

273
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:11,180
I cannot do that.

274
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:13,680
I looked into it,

275
00:16:13,880 --> 00:16:16,210
and that money you took to buy
a building in Seongsu-dong...

276
00:16:16,510 --> 00:16:18,150
went straight
to paying off your debts.

277
00:16:18,220 --> 00:16:20,050
Did you do a background check on me?

278
00:16:21,450 --> 00:16:24,250
If I could even abandon
my own daughter,

279
00:16:24,960 --> 00:16:27,020
what wouldn't I do?

280
00:16:29,290 --> 00:16:31,060
From now on, you will take
an allowance from me...

281
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:32,360
every month on the dot.

282
00:16:33,900 --> 00:16:36,000
If you do not like it,
the deal is off.

283
00:16:36,400 --> 00:16:39,200
Do you think I came all the way here
for pocket change?

284
00:16:41,740 --> 00:16:42,740
Hey.

285
00:16:43,010 --> 00:16:45,240
Did you forget what kind of business
I used to run?

286
00:16:46,110 --> 00:16:48,650
You think you can look down on me...

287
00:16:48,710 --> 00:16:50,510
just because you managed
to seduce a rich man...

288
00:16:50,750 --> 00:16:52,450
and sit in that fancy position?

289
00:16:53,520 --> 00:16:55,120
Just because I worked
in the nightlife business,

290
00:16:55,220 --> 00:16:56,290
do you think
you can walk all over me?

291
00:16:59,020 --> 00:17:00,020
I will be seeing you.

292
00:17:06,360 --> 00:17:07,400
So annoying.

293
00:17:09,730 --> 00:17:10,900
Should I just get rid of her?

294
00:17:12,770 --> 00:17:14,370
Color code 151512,

295
00:17:14,870 --> 00:17:15,910
Dusty Mauve.

296
00:17:16,670 --> 00:17:18,610
This one is red...

297
00:17:25,650 --> 00:17:26,720
(Mom, I missed you, so I came home.)

298
00:17:26,720 --> 00:17:28,690
(Where are you? Did you have dinner?
Come home soon. I will be waiting.)

299
00:17:28,690 --> 00:17:29,820
Why isn't she reading it?

300
00:17:33,660 --> 00:17:36,560
Excuse me, Da Mi.
Did you memorize what I told you to?

301
00:17:37,760 --> 00:17:39,460
Yes, I have almost got it all down.

302
00:17:39,800 --> 00:17:40,960
(Aunt Ri Ja)

303
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:42,200
Just a moment, please.

304
00:17:49,540 --> 00:17:51,980
How many times
has she stepped away today?

305
00:17:54,610 --> 00:17:55,980
Is she job hunting?

306
00:17:58,720 --> 00:18:00,850
Auntie, is Mom not back yet?

307
00:18:03,690 --> 00:18:04,690
All right.

308
00:18:05,760 --> 00:18:08,960
Well, when she gets back,
could you please text me?

309
00:18:09,830 --> 00:18:10,830
Okay.

310
00:18:29,710 --> 00:18:30,750
Excuse me, Kang Da Mi.

311
00:18:31,110 --> 00:18:32,120
Yes, Head Designer Cha?

312
00:18:32,650 --> 00:18:35,320
You seem to be leaving
your desk a lot today.

313
00:18:35,950 --> 00:18:38,120
I am sorry,
I had to make a phone call.

314
00:18:38,520 --> 00:18:40,020
Did you actually come here to work?

315
00:18:40,390 --> 00:18:42,760
Are you going to show up tomorrow
like normal?

316
00:18:44,230 --> 00:18:45,700
What do you mean by that?

317
00:18:45,960 --> 00:18:48,100
It is not like
I was purposely trying...

318
00:18:48,170 --> 00:18:50,400
to keep count of
how many times you stepped away.

319
00:18:50,470 --> 00:18:52,240
Just from when
I started counting today,

320
00:18:52,300 --> 00:18:54,040
this is already your eighth time
leaving your desk.

321
00:18:54,100 --> 00:18:55,240
The eighth time.

322
00:18:55,510 --> 00:18:58,410
If you're looking for another job,

323
00:18:58,440 --> 00:19:00,210
I would rather
you just tell me honestly.

324
00:19:00,310 --> 00:19:01,910
I am a busy person too.

325
00:19:03,180 --> 00:19:05,180
It is not like that,
Head Designer Cha.

326
00:19:05,650 --> 00:19:07,580
It is not? Are you sure?

327
00:19:08,350 --> 00:19:09,850
Yes, absolutely.

328
00:19:09,920 --> 00:19:11,360
It is just that
something came up at home...

329
00:19:11,420 --> 00:19:15,590
Stop. Look, I have things going on
at home too.

330
00:19:16,460 --> 00:19:19,760
But when I am at work,
I focus only on work, right?

331
00:19:19,830 --> 00:19:23,230
So I need you to put your work
first, too, Kang Da Mi.

332
00:19:23,970 --> 00:19:24,970
Yes, sir.

333
00:19:34,010 --> 00:19:37,310
Now that I've seen
the outsourced staff...

334
00:19:37,450 --> 00:19:41,420
get fixed-term contracts
and bonuses with my own eyes,

335
00:19:42,020 --> 00:19:44,390
I will get going.

336
00:19:45,260 --> 00:19:47,860
- Let us head home together, Mother.
- What?

337
00:19:49,090 --> 00:19:50,990
You are leaving work already?

338
00:19:51,830 --> 00:19:52,830
Pardon?

339
00:19:54,770 --> 00:19:55,770
No.

340
00:19:56,500 --> 00:19:58,700
You spent all afternoon
at the office...

341
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,700
getting briefed
and touring the place,

342
00:20:00,740 --> 00:20:02,710
so I thought you must be
exhausted, Mother.

343
00:20:03,240 --> 00:20:05,040
I should take you home.

344
00:20:07,210 --> 00:20:09,050
Jun Sung used to say,

345
00:20:10,280 --> 00:20:12,150
"Mother, I have too much work
at the office,"

346
00:20:12,720 --> 00:20:16,420
"so I cannot take you home.
Please go home first."

347
00:20:16,850 --> 00:20:18,220
"I will see you at home."

348
00:20:19,390 --> 00:20:20,390
That is what he would say.

349
00:20:21,630 --> 00:20:25,400
You still have a long way to go
to catch up to your brother.

350
00:20:28,800 --> 00:20:31,000
"No matter how hard I try,
I can't move up."

351
00:20:31,700 --> 00:20:34,740
"I will never be acknowledged
by the head of the family."

352
00:20:35,740 --> 00:20:37,440
That sense of limitation
and deprivation.

353
00:20:38,580 --> 00:20:42,010
I don't want Do Yun
to feel that way anymore.

354
00:20:43,250 --> 00:20:45,250
At least our Seung Yun...

355
00:20:45,520 --> 00:20:48,720
takes after his father, Jun Sung,
which is a great relief.

356
00:20:49,250 --> 00:20:50,650
I asked around,

357
00:20:50,820 --> 00:20:53,520
and everyone's giving him
such high praise.

358
00:20:54,760 --> 00:20:58,730
Mother,
Do Yun is doing just as well.

359
00:20:59,100 --> 00:21:02,430
When did I ever say Do Yun wasn't?

360
00:21:02,670 --> 00:21:05,000
The ones who built Hwanggeum Apparel
into what it is today...

361
00:21:05,070 --> 00:21:08,670
are Do Yun and his mother.
They've done that for years.

362
00:21:09,040 --> 00:21:10,040
So?

363
00:21:14,710 --> 00:21:15,710
Well,

364
00:21:16,380 --> 00:21:19,180
you still cling only
to my late brother,

365
00:21:19,850 --> 00:21:22,320
and at times like this, it hurts.
I feel upset, too.

366
00:21:24,190 --> 00:21:25,220
What did you say?

367
00:21:25,690 --> 00:21:27,620
After my brother and his wife
passed away,

368
00:21:27,790 --> 00:21:30,190
the ones who stayed
by your side were us.

369
00:21:30,430 --> 00:21:31,830
Do Yun's mother and I.

370
00:21:32,330 --> 00:21:34,430
So why do you only look
for my brother...

371
00:21:34,500 --> 00:21:35,800
and only caring about Seung Yun?

372
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:39,470
You know how hard she worked,
don't you, Mother?

373
00:21:39,870 --> 00:21:41,370
For both the company and the family.

374
00:21:42,040 --> 00:21:44,540
Why won't you give her credit
for what she did?

375
00:21:45,280 --> 00:21:47,740
All right. From your perspective,

376
00:21:48,380 --> 00:21:50,750
those times must have felt hurtful.

377
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:55,190
However,

378
00:21:56,120 --> 00:21:59,220
now that we're talking
about CEO Jeon,

379
00:21:59,660 --> 00:22:02,560
there's something I'd like to ask.

380
00:22:03,490 --> 00:22:04,730
Yes, go ahead.

381
00:22:05,500 --> 00:22:06,960
About the past,

382
00:22:07,130 --> 00:22:10,570
when Do Yun's mother lived
under the name Jeon Jin Sook,

383
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:13,240
how much do you actually know?

384
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:18,910
- Well, that is...
- All you told me...

385
00:22:18,980 --> 00:22:22,110
was that you dropped by
a design boutique...

386
00:22:22,310 --> 00:22:25,120
where she worked as a junior
employee, and you met.

387
00:22:25,120 --> 00:22:27,250
That's all I've ever heard.

388
00:22:27,650 --> 00:22:30,150
How did she live back then?

389
00:22:32,060 --> 00:22:33,160
Mother.

390
00:22:33,660 --> 00:22:36,730
I don't really...

391
00:23:08,060 --> 00:23:09,360
(Kang Dae Chi, Second Son)

392
00:23:09,430 --> 00:23:10,930
(Kang Gang Nam, Eldest Son,
Kang Da Mi, My Youngest)

393
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:16,230
(Kang Da Mi)

394
00:23:16,300 --> 00:23:19,700
Mom. I missed you, so I came home.

395
00:23:20,070 --> 00:23:21,740
Come home soon. I will be waiting.

396
00:23:26,710 --> 00:23:28,350
Mom, why haven't you been
answering your phone?

397
00:23:28,410 --> 00:23:31,850
Do you know how worried I was?
And the rest of the family, too.

398
00:23:32,120 --> 00:23:33,150
Were you, sweetie?

399
00:23:35,450 --> 00:23:41,090
I was feeling down,
so I came out to get some fresh air.

400
00:23:41,560 --> 00:23:42,690
You were worried,

401
00:23:44,430 --> 00:23:45,730
and so was everyone else.

402
00:23:46,100 --> 00:23:47,700
Of course we were, Mom.

403
00:23:48,170 --> 00:23:50,430
If your family doesn't worry
about you, who will?

404
00:23:51,200 --> 00:23:52,400
I'm sorry, sweetie.

405
00:23:53,500 --> 00:23:56,170
I'm heading home today.

406
00:23:57,310 --> 00:23:58,310
By the way,

407
00:23:59,680 --> 00:24:02,810
I heard you bought a yellow dress.
Is that true?

408
00:24:03,510 --> 00:24:04,850
What?

409
00:24:07,020 --> 00:24:09,020
Yes, I did.

410
00:24:09,150 --> 00:24:11,320
Good for you, Mom. That's wonderful.

411
00:24:12,260 --> 00:24:15,790
I thought you'd nag me
for buying something pricey.

412
00:24:16,790 --> 00:24:20,260
- What got into my thrifty daughter?
- I've always wanted you...

413
00:24:20,260 --> 00:24:23,670
to dress up nicely.
Ever since I was little,

414
00:24:23,670 --> 00:24:25,340
I nagged you
to take care of yourself.

415
00:24:25,570 --> 00:24:26,600
Did you forget?

416
00:24:28,370 --> 00:24:30,440
By the way, Gang Nam said...

417
00:24:30,510 --> 00:24:33,310
he saw you walking with a man.

418
00:24:34,140 --> 00:24:35,150
Who is he?

419
00:24:36,080 --> 00:24:38,650
What? Well...

420
00:24:39,980 --> 00:24:41,350
He is just an acquaintance.

421
00:24:42,050 --> 00:24:43,050
A friend.

422
00:24:43,750 --> 00:24:45,460
I heard you have
a male acquaintance too.

423
00:24:46,420 --> 00:24:49,230
Did you really go dancing
with that friend of yours?

424
00:24:49,990 --> 00:24:51,860
I doubt that is true.

425
00:24:52,760 --> 00:24:53,930
I did dance.

426
00:24:54,460 --> 00:24:55,470
Really.

427
00:24:57,600 --> 00:25:00,670
Sweetheart.
You know I love plays, right?

428
00:25:03,040 --> 00:25:04,240
I even saw a play.

429
00:25:05,140 --> 00:25:07,310
Really? Did you like it?

430
00:25:09,410 --> 00:25:10,410
Yes.

431
00:25:11,110 --> 00:25:12,180
I really enjoyed it.

432
00:25:14,450 --> 00:25:15,450
I...

433
00:25:17,250 --> 00:25:18,660
I was truly happy.

434
00:25:20,920 --> 00:25:22,930
I am so happy for you, Mom.

435
00:25:23,190 --> 00:25:25,230
Do whatever you want.
Enjoy yourself as much as you like.

436
00:25:26,530 --> 00:25:28,600
All you did was work hard
at the restaurant...

437
00:25:28,970 --> 00:25:31,300
to raise all of us.

438
00:25:32,800 --> 00:25:33,800
Really?

439
00:25:35,010 --> 00:25:36,040
Is that really okay?

440
00:25:38,680 --> 00:25:40,080
I do not have much time, though.

441
00:25:41,910 --> 00:25:43,450
I think I will only get busier now.

442
00:25:44,450 --> 00:25:45,550
Of course.

443
00:25:45,980 --> 00:25:48,520
You should live your life
doing what you love, Mom.

444
00:25:48,720 --> 00:25:50,350
If you only care for us
all the time,

445
00:25:50,450 --> 00:25:52,060
you will make yourself sick.

446
00:25:53,360 --> 00:25:55,760
Just make sure to answer your phone.

447
00:25:56,830 --> 00:26:00,000
Whenever you do not pick up,
I cannot even focus on work.

448
00:26:02,970 --> 00:26:05,070
Okay. I will always answer
from now on.

449
00:26:06,100 --> 00:26:07,240
Watch out for cars, sweetie.

450
00:26:08,100 --> 00:26:09,540
I will call you when I get home.

451
00:27:15,170 --> 00:27:16,240
Ms. Jo.

452
00:27:21,110 --> 00:27:22,150
Dr. Ju.

453
00:27:25,520 --> 00:27:26,680
What do I do?

454
00:27:28,150 --> 00:27:31,550
What should I do, Dr. Ju?

455
00:27:49,610 --> 00:27:51,440
(Mission: Mompossible)

456
00:28:08,060 --> 00:28:09,860
Just because you pulled off
one clever move,

457
00:28:09,960 --> 00:28:13,000
- don't let it get to your head.
- I am happy, that's true,

458
00:28:13,430 --> 00:28:15,070
but I am not making
more of it than that.

459
00:28:15,530 --> 00:28:18,030
They said he is definitely here.
Why is he not coming out?

460
00:28:19,240 --> 00:28:20,240
Don't tell me...

461
00:28:20,640 --> 00:28:23,010
Mom is drinking coffee...

462
00:28:23,170 --> 00:28:25,510
- and reading a book.
- Seriously, what is wrong with her?

463
00:28:25,680 --> 00:28:27,280
Why aren't you eating, Kang Da Mi?

464
00:28:27,410 --> 00:28:29,210
Excuse me.
I need to use the restroom.

465
00:28:31,580 --> 00:28:33,580
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
